  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(-2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T({v}_{1}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =-2T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] & =-2T({v}_{1})+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ -2T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ -2T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{-2}[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
